.TH EQNORBITALTEST 1
.SH NAME
eqnorbitaltest \- test a real command-module Danby model end to end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eqnorbitaltest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Eqnorbitaltest
fetches
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)'s
own spec text through its real in-process
.B run()
seam - the same call
.IR appl/temple/eqnorbital.b
(the harness) makes, matching
.IR hoc (2)'s
own already-established
.B run(argv):
.RI ( string , int )
convention - then parses and drives it with an INDEPENDENTLY WRITTEN
copy of the same small grammar, not by reaching into the harness's own
internals (not reachable from outside its own module type anyway -
Dis's
.B load
type-checks against a compiled module's own declared interface, not
whatever shape a caller asks for). Two independent implementations of
the same grammar reaching the same known-correct physics is a
stronger check than one implementation calling itself twice.
.PP
Checks both components of the
.RB \*(lq derivative
vx\*(rq/\*(lqderivative vy\*(rq
lines (central gravity plus atmospheric drag, the same numbers
verified before this model became a command module) and both
.B observable
values, all pulled from the model's own currently-printed spec text,
not a copy pasted into this test.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/eqnorbitaltest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-aerobraking (1),
.IR eqn2hoc (2),
.IR hoc (2),
.IR danbyeqnall (1)
.SH BUGS
Only pulls out
.BR param / derivative / eq
lines - not a full reimplementation of every directive
.IR appl/temple/eqnorbital.b 's
own grammar has
.RB ( bodylabels / mass / state / observable
aren't needed for this specific check, though
.B observable
values are cross-checked indirectly since this model's two
observables are themselves bare
.B eq
names).
